# 🥐 French Bakery — Sales Prediction by Machine Learning

### Machine Learning | Ironhack Data Analytics Bootcamp

## Project Overview

This project uses Machine Learning to predict **daily sales quantities for individual bakery products** based on historical sales data.

**Business Goal:** Help bakeries improve production planning, reduce food waste, and maintain product availability.

## Dataset

- **Period:** January 2021 – September 2022
- **Products:** 26 bakery items (originally 149)
- **ML-ready dataset:** 13,467 observations (originally 234,005)
- **Target Variable:** Quantity sold per product per day

## Project Workflow

1. **Data Cleaning & EDA** — Explore sales patterns and prepare the dataset.
2. **Feature Engineering** — Create calendar features and historical sales indicators.
3. **Model Training** — Compare 7 regression models using a chronological 80/20 train/test split.
4. **Hyperparameter Tuning** — Optimize the best-performing models using GridSearchCV.
5. **Model Evaluation** — Evaluate prediction accuracy and extract business insights.

## Final Model & Performance

**Selected Model: Bagging Regressor**

| Metric          | Result         |
| --------------- | -------------- |
| MAE             | **5.86 units** |
| RMSE            | 14.79 units    |
| R² Score        | 0.95           |
| Baseline MAE    | 8.80 units     |
| MAE Improvement | **\~33%**      |

The model predicts daily sales with an average absolute error of approximately **6 units per product per day**.

## Business Insights

- **Production Planning:** Better estimates of daily product demand.
- **Waste Reduction:** Potential to reduce overproduction.
- **Product Availability:** Support decisions about how much to prepare.

These are potential benefits; actual business impact has not been measured.

## Tools & Technologies

Python · Pandas · Scikit-learn · Matplotlib · Jupyter Notebook

## Limitations

The model uses historical sales data and requires further validation on new, unseen data before real-world deployment. The test set was also used during initial model comparison, so final performance is not a fully independent evaluation.

